@startuml client_connection_switch_to_stop_state_activity
title ClientConnection - shared stop finalization

start
:SwitchToStopState();
note right
    Entry conditions asserted in debug builds:
    state_ == kStopping, stop_reason_ != kNone,
    and execution on the engine callback thread.
    A caller has already claimed the stop transition.
end note
if (lifetime_.RetirementPending()?) then (yes)
    :Initial cancellation is already complete;
else (no)
    :Begin the initial cancellation phase;
    :Disable the endpoint disconnect callback;
    :CleanUpOwner(this);
    :sends_.CancelPending();
    if (lifetime_.CancellationFinished()?) then (yes)
        :No operation remains after cancellation;
    else (no)
        :Return in kStopping without closing the descriptor;
        note right
            The last Operation destructor schedules
            disconnection_command_ to reenter this procedure.
            There is no polling or wait inside Restart().
        end note
        stop
    endif
endif
:FinishStopState();
:lifetime_.RetireDescriptor();
if (The detached descriptor is valid?) then (yes)
    :CloseClientConnection(detached descriptor) without lifetime_.mutex_;
else (no)
    :No descriptor to close;
endif

if (state_callback is empty?) then (yes)
    :Publish kStopped;
else (no)
    :Keep a local shared reference to CallbackContext;
    :Lock context.finalize_mutex;
    :Publish kStopped;
    :Invoke state_callback(kStopped);
    note right
        Restart() can reenter kStarting before this callback returns.
        Destruction releases the connection's context reference.
        The local reference keeps the callback and mutex alive.
        No connection members are accessed after this invocation.
    end note
    :Return from the stopped-state callback;
    :Unlock context.finalize_mutex;
    :Release the local shared reference;
endif
stop

legend
    Shared cleanup reached from API stopping, failed connection
    establishment, and endpoint-disconnect dispatch.
    This procedure does not select or reset the stop reason.
    The caller's gate owns stopping for the current lifecycle.
    Cancellation runs once; a deferred entry skips that initial phase.
    Cancellation and retirement belong to separate helpers, not facade locks.
    Descriptor closure follows all registered send termination bookkeeping.
    Close itself may block: no finite QNX IPC termination bound is assumed.
endlegend

@enduml